WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.318
Telemetry signals answer different operational questions.

00:00:02.318 --> 00:00:04.535
Metrics summarize numeric behavior over time.

00:00:04.535 --> 00:00:08.970
They are useful for latency, error rate, throughput, request volume, queue depth,

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.557
GPU utilization, memory pressure, and similar trends.

00:00:11.557 --> 00:00:14.514
Metrics are compact and easy to alert on,

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:18.580
but they usually do not explain the full story by themselves.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.797
Logs record discrete events and details.

00:00:20.797 --> 00:00:25.232
A log entry can explain that a route selected a model version,

00:00:25.232 --> 00:00:29.298
a retrieval call timed out, a pipeline job skipped a source,

00:00:29.298 --> 00:00:31.146
or an administrative change occurred.

00:00:31.146 --> 00:00:35.581
Logs are valuable during investigation, but they need structure and data discipline.

00:00:35.581 --> 00:00:40.386
They should provide useful context without turning sensitive request content into permanent records.

00:00:40.386 --> 00:00:42.234
Traces connect work across services.

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:44.082
In a distributed AI workflow,

00:00:44.082 --> 00:00:49.995
a trace can show that a request moved from an API gateway to an inference service,

00:00:49.995 --> 00:00:52.952
then to retrieval, storage, and a downstream service.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:58.496
Traces help teams distinguish time spent in application logic from time spent waiting on dependencies,

00:00:58.496 --> 00:00:59.974
scheduling, or network calls.

00:00:59.974 --> 00:01:03.670
Events and audit records capture important state changes, policy decisions,

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:05.518
administrative actions, and security-relevant activity.

00:01:05.518 --> 00:01:10.323
Profiles and health checks add another view by showing performance characteristics and readiness.

00:01:10.323 --> 00:01:12.171
No single signal is enough.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:17.345
A useful operating picture combines metrics for trends, logs for detail, traces for flow,

00:01:17.345 --> 00:01:21.780
events for change, audits for accountability, and health checks for current state.
